{"person_id":"gene-simmons","name":"Gene Simmons","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Rock musician, bassist","birth_year":1949,"age_at_milestone":23,"milestone_by_age_26":"Co-founded the rock band KISS in January 1973 at age 23, releasing three studio albums by age 26 including the debut 'Kiss' (Feb 1974) and 'Dressed to Kill' (Mar 1975).","early_history_summary":"Born Chaim Witz in Haifa, Israel to a Hungarian Jewish Holocaust-survivor mother; immigrated to Queens, NYC at age 8. Played bass in teenage bands, met Paul Stanley in the early 1970s, and formed Wicked Lester (1970-1972) which secured but lost an Epic Records deal. Dissolved Wicked Lester and co-founded KISS in January 1973 with Stanley, Peter Criss, and Ace Frehley, adopting the 'Demon' persona.","primary_leverage_engine":"Stage spectacle and shock rock persona","normalized_primary_engine":"Distribution / audience","secondary_engine":"Complementary partnership with Paul Stanley","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":2,"structural_wave_score":2,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":11,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Born to Hungarian Jewish refugee parents; mother survived Nazi concentration camps. Family was 'dirt poor' in Israel; parents divorced when he was 8; immigrated to US with mother who worked to support them.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":0,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":2,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":1,"inherited_access_stack_count":4,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":1,"all_documented_early_condition_count":4,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"High-trust peer team","primary_early_advantage_tags":"complementary partnership with Paul Stanley, NYC rock scene immersion, immigrant adversity, shock rock wave","evidence_summary":"Gene Simmons (born Chaim Witz) co-founded KISS in January 1973 at age 23 with Paul Stanley, releasing their debut album by February 1974 and three albums by age 26. He grew up poor in Queens after immigrating from Israel with his Holocaust-survivor mother. His key advantage was the complementary partnership with Stanley and immersion in the NYC rock scene, though no family resources or domain connections are documented. The mid-1970s shock rock/glam wave provided structural tailwind.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene_Simmons","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene_Simmons","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/gene-simmons-mn0000200968","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicked_Lester","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KISS_(band)"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
