{"person_id":"diane-keaton","name":"Diane Keaton","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Actress","birth_year":1946,"age_at_milestone":23,"milestone_by_age_26":"Earned a Tony Award nomination for Best Featured Actress in a Play for Woody Allen's 'Play It Again, Sam' on Broadway in 1969 at age 23, and was cast in The Godfather (1972) by age 26.","early_history_summary":"Born Diane Hall in Los Angeles, she studied acting at Santa Ana College and the Neighborhood Playhouse in NYC under Sanford Meisner. She joined the original Broadway production of Hair (1968) and was cast by Woody Allen in Play It Again, Sam (1969), earning a Tony nomination. She made her screen debut in Lovers and Other Strangers (1970) and was cast in The Godfather (1972).","primary_leverage_engine":"Comic acting talent and timing","normalized_primary_engine":"Product / domain insight","secondary_engine":"Woody Allen collaboration","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":9,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Born to Dorothy Keaton, a homemaker and amateur photographer, and Jack Hall, a civil engineer and real estate broker. Mother won 'Mrs. Los Angeles' pageant, which Keaton said inspired her theatrical impulse.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources; no direct entertainment industry family connections found.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":1,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":1,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":0,"inherited_access_stack_count":5,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":0,"all_documented_early_condition_count":5,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Institutional ecosystem acceleration","primary_early_advantage_tags":"Neighborhood Playhouse training, Broadway access, Woody Allen collaboration, NYC theater immersion","evidence_summary":"Diane Keaton earned a Tony Award nomination at age 23 for Play It Again, Sam (1969) on Broadway, and was cast in The Godfather by 26. She trained at the Neighborhood Playhouse under Sanford Meisner and joined the Broadway ensemble of Hair (1968). Her mother's amateur photography and pageant win inspired her theatrical interest, but no family entertainment-industry connections or financial platform are documented. The Woody Allen collaboration was a key early catalyst.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diane_Keaton","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diane_Keaton","https://www.ibdb.com/broadway-cast-staff/diane-keaton-47603","https://www.biography.com/actors/diane-keaton","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000473/bio/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
