{"person_id":"juan-alberto-schiaffino","name":"Juan Alberto Schiaffino","cohort_group":"Athletes","category":"Soccer player","birth_year":1925,"age_at_milestone":25,"milestone_by_age_26":"Won the 1950 FIFA World Cup with Uruguay at age 25, scoring the equalizer in the final against Brazil (the Maracanazo), and was a key player for Peñarol with multiple league titles by that age.","early_history_summary":"Born in Montevideo, Schiaffino played football in neighborhood parks before joining Peñarol's youth team at 17, becoming a first-teamer by 18 (1943). He debuted for Uruguay's national team at 20 (1945) and became a central figure in Peñarol's dominant 'La Maquina del 49' team. At 25, he scored the equalizer in the 1950 World Cup final against Brazil.","primary_leverage_engine":"Early specialization in football","normalized_primary_engine":"Early specialization / prior reps","secondary_engine":"Football intelligence and playmaking","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":2,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":2,"total_leverage_score":11,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Born in Montevideo; his brother Raúl Schiaffino was already a striker at Peñarol and brought Juan to the club at age 18. Family financial background not extensively documented in reviewed sources.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Brother Raúl was a professional footballer at Peñarol who facilitated Juan's entry to the club; no evidence of parental football connections.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":1,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":2,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":1,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":0,"inherited_access_stack_count":5,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":1,"all_documented_early_condition_count":5,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Elite performance pipeline","primary_early_advantage_tags":"Peñarol youth system, brother's club connection, Montevideo football culture, early professional debut, World Cup winner at 25","evidence_summary":"Juan Alberto Schiaffino won the 1950 FIFA World Cup with Uruguay at age 25, scoring the equalizer in the famous Maracanazo final against Brazil. He joined Peñarol's youth team at 17 and was a first-teamer by 18 (1943), debuting for Uruguay at 20 (1945). His brother Raúl, already a Peñarol player, facilitated his entry to the club. He was a key figure in Peñarol's dominant 1949 league-winning team. Family financial background is not documented in reviewed sources.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Alberto_Schiaffino","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Alberto_Schiaffino","https://backpagefootball.com/world-cup-legends-uruguay-juan-alberto-schiaffino/77774/","https://www.planetworldcup.com/LEGENDS/schiaffi.html","https://uruguaylatecap.com/2021/07/28/juan-alberto-schiaffino/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
